<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Javier Milei</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">b. 1970</span> · <a href="/centuries/21st-century">21st century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Javier Milei is an Argentine economist and politician who became president of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/argentina">Argentina</a> in December 2023. A libertarian television commentator first elected to Congress in 2021, he won the presidency amid <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/inflation">inflation</a> above 100 per cent a year, promising to cut back the state drastically. His government sharply reduced public spending and brought inflation down.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/javier-milei.jpg" alt="Javier Milei" width="320" height="427" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: The White House · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Javier_Milei_in_pull-aside_meeting_at_the_United_Nations_Headquarters_(3x4_cropped).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
